# Copy to .env.local and fill in your own Supabase project.
# Only PUBLIC values belong here. Never put a service-role / secret key in a VITE_ variable.
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-PROJECT.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=your-publishable-or-anon-key

# ── Keyless central subscription auto-sync (optional) ────────────────────────
# Leave both blank and myClinic keeps licensing itself locally, exactly as before.
# Set both and the clinic's plan, seat limits and expiry come from the central
# subscription service — no licence key, no RSA key pair and no Edge Function.
# The browser calls ONE public PostgREST RPC (sync_clinic_subscription) with the
# owner's email, this deployment's origin and a per-browser device id, then seals
# the answer in localStorage so a lost connection does not stop the clinic.
#
# What belongs here: the central project's URL and its PUBLISHABLE key. Nothing
# else. A VITE_ variable is compiled into the bundle and served to every visitor,
# so `sb_secret_…` or a service-role key is refused at load time — by the app and
# by the Pages workflow.
# VITE_CENTRAL_SUPABASE_URL=https://YOUR-CENTRAL-PROJECT.supabase.co
# VITE_CENTRAL_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=sb_publishable_…
